# ============================================================
# Triibholz — deployment settings. Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and edit.
#
# docker-compose reads these. With no .env at all the app runs exactly as it
# always has: accounts OFF, simulated sign-in, nothing authorized. That is the
# right state for local development and for the test suites.
#
# The server REFUSES TO START on a bad combination rather than quietly
# weakening sign-in (server/config.js), so a typo here is a loud failure, not a
# silent one.
# ============================================================

# ---------- local development (the default: leave everything unset) ----------
# The app is at http://localhost:8088. Demo personas, no passkeys, no server
# authorization. Nothing below is needed.


# ---------- production: https://thplay.ch ----------
# Uncomment ONLY when the domain actually serves this app over https.
#
# RP_ID is the domain passkeys belong to, and it is PERMANENT: a credential made
# for one RP_ID cannot be moved to another. Changing it later means every coach
# and every parent registers again. No scheme, no port, no path.
#
# APP_ORIGINS is the exact address(es) the app is opened from. Every POST must
# arrive with one of these as its Origin, and each must be on RP_ID.
#
# ACCOUNTS=1
# RP_ID=thplay.ch
# APP_ORIGINS=https://thplay.ch
#
# If www.thplay.ch is also served (rather than redirected), add it — a passkey
# made on thplay.ch works on its subdomains, but the Origin check does not guess:
# APP_ORIGINS=https://thplay.ch,https://www.thplay.ch

# Behind a tunnel, nginx must be told which peer may be believed about the
# visitor's real address — otherwise every visitor shares one rate-limit bucket
# and one club's sign-ins throttle each other. This is the tunnel container's
# address on the app's Docker network (deploy/nginx-real-ip.sh,
# scripts/test-nginx-realip.sh).
# TRUSTED_PROXY=172.19.0.4


# ---------- staging ----------
# A staging hostname gets its OWN RP_ID so rehearsing sign-in, pairing and
# recovery cannot mint passkeys that work against production:
# ACCOUNTS=1
# RP_ID=staging.thplay.ch
# APP_ORIGINS=https://staging.thplay.ch


# ---------- what is NOT possible, on purpose ----------
# Production and localhost together: APP_ORIGINS entries must all be on RP_ID,
# and http is only allowed for localhost with DEV=1 and RP_ID=localhost. So the
# moment accounts point at thplay.ch, http://localhost:8088 is no longer a way in.
# Develop with accounts off, or with RP_ID=localhost and DEV=1.
